1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:22,951
"Nigga, why this invitation got two seats and one exit?" Tank held the
card up to the light. Rosa took it from him. "Because somebody thinks
they're clever." "I don't like clever niggas with buildings." "You
love Aiden." "That nigga breaks his own buildings. That's different."
"How?" "Nigga breaks a building, you can see him coming out with
everybody who was in it.

2
00:00:23,201 --> 00:00:40,521
This nigga sends invitations and makes you count the exits." Rosa
looked at the card again. "That's a fair distinction." "Nigga, I know
my favorite dangerous man from a damn appointment." I was standing in
front of the mirror while Shawna tied my black tie.

3
00:00:40,771 --> 00:00:58,889
She had refused three hotel stylists and told a fourth that if he
touched her hair again she would make him explain it to the ocean.
Tonight she wore red. The kind of red that made a nigga forget blue
had ever accomplished anything. "You looking at the tie?" she asked.

4
00:00:59,139 --> 00:01:22,709
"I'm looking near it." "Try higher." "Baby, you gave me a difficult
route." She pulled the knot snug and kissed me. Behind us, Tank
groaned. "Nigga, we got a betrayal appointment. Can y'all flirt in the
car like normal dangerous people?" The Palace of Mirrors stood on a
little island reached by a bridge of white stone. Every window
reflected the water.

5
00:01:22,959 --> 00:01:46,560
Every guard wore silver. I had started to notice a pattern: the worse
the man inside, the more somebody polished the outside. Rusk greeted
us at the entrance with his bandaged hand tucked behind his back.
"Captain. Madame." "You walking better," I said. "I owe you my life."
"Start with good seats." He actually smiled. Nigga, I had improved him
too.

6
00:01:46,810 --> 00:02:12,363
Inside, the couples stood beneath a ceiling of turning mirrors. Old
kings with old queens. Young claimants with new girlfriends. One
prince with two wives who looked more interested in talking to each
other than standing beside him. All of us adults, all dressed like
consequences had been invited somewhere else. Vesper waited beside a
raised platform. Zero stood at its center.

7
00:02:12,613 --> 00:02:35,477
"Tonight," he said, "we discover what each of you values more than
victory." I leaned toward Shawna. "Nigga finna discover how much I
value dinner." She bit back a laugh. Zero's gaze found us. "Some men
are loudest when they are uncertain." "Some niggas build a mirror
palace because one reflection ain't agreeing with them." A sound went
through the room.

8
00:02:35,727 --> 00:03:02,555
Half laughter, half men trying not to be seen laughing. Zero's
expression didn't change. "The pairs will enter separately. Each will
be offered a private bargain. Wealth. Authority. Freedom from a debt.
The power to decide who leaves victorious." "And nobody gets hurt?"
Lady Orsini asked. "Unless they choose very unwisely." Her husband
sighed. "Darling, perhaps we should have stayed for dessert." "We did.

9
00:03:02,805 --> 00:03:25,090
They interrupted it." Shawna put her hand in mine. "Whatever he offers
you, make him say the price out loud." "Whatever the nigga offers you,
tell him your husband already got it in another color." She smiled.
"Even the ocean?" "Nigga, especially the ocean." A servant took me
through a mirrored door. Another took Shawna through the one beside
it.

10
00:03:25,340 --> 00:03:47,900
We let go at the same time, not because either of us wanted to, but
because there are men who can smell hesitation and I wasn't feeding
this one anything. My room contained a chair, a table, and a view of
the harbor. On the table lay the deed to an estate. Beside it, a
photograph of Shawna performing at the island celebration.

11
00:03:48,150 --> 00:04:11,112
Zero entered through a side door. "You collect extraordinary women,"
he said. "Nigga, I married one. You collecting terrible openings." He
sat without inviting me to. I sat anyway. "Your wife has talent. Real
talent. A world tour could make her independent of everything you
are." "She already independent of my permission.

12
00:04:11,362 --> 00:04:31,396
Nigga, you brought my wife's photograph in here and still ain't looked
at the woman in it." "And if independence takes her away from you?" I
looked at the photograph. Her head tilted back, her mouth open on a
note, her whole body giving something to the crowd that I loved partly
because it didn't belong only to me.

13
00:04:31,646 --> 00:04:51,924
"Then I buy a ticket." Zero waited. "Front row," I added. "Nigga,
don't get cheap in your imagination." He moved the deed closer. "This
estate includes the city's western harbor. Its ships. Its clubs. Its
protection. All I ask is that you withdraw from the final Crown round.

14
00:04:52,174 --> 00:05:16,177
Your wife receives the opera house outright." "She pick her own
songs?" "Of course." "Then she's gonna sing about the nigga who lost
his crown to me. You sure you want that in your building?" For the
first time, he showed irritation without covering it immediately. "You
confuse defiance with strength." "Nigga, you keep confusing furniture
with a marriage. You got deeds on a table.

15
00:05:16,426 --> 00:05:38,722
This nigga has a woman downstairs who knows how he takes his coffee
and still bothers asking how he slept. Which one you think I came this
far to keep?" He leaned back. "Very well. The next door leads to your
partner. One of you must surrender your token before it opens. The
other keeps the prize." He placed a gold token on the table.

16
00:05:38,972 --> 00:05:58,097
Mine bore a crown. Through the wall, faintly, I heard Shawna laugh.
Nigga, that laugh saved me five minutes of wondering. "What you offer
her?" Zero stood. "You may ask her if you reach her." After he left, a
voice instructed me to place my token into a slot beside the door.

17
00:05:58,346 --> 00:06:21,121
A little screen showed two cars on opposite ends of a track suspended
above the palace's indoor pool. In one car sat Shawna. In the other
was an empty driver's seat waiting for me. I looked at the screen.
"Nigga, this is a date with extra nonsense." The door opened. The
track was a long silver curve beneath the turning mirrors.

18
00:06:21,371 --> 00:06:42,792
Half of it vanished behind a wall. The cars were small open racers,
beautiful and ridiculous, with polished steering wheels and almost no
room for a man to hide his feelings. Shawna lifted her hand when she
saw me. "They offer you a harbor?" "You an opera house?" "And a
separation agreement." The room went quiet.

19
00:06:43,042 --> 00:07:02,614
I looked up at the balcony where Zero had reappeared. "Nigga." Just
that. He looked down calmly. Shawna raised a folded paper. "I wrote a
review on the back." "What it say?" "That your mother raised you
better than his did." Tank's laugh came through a doorway somewhere
behind the spectators.

20
00:07:02,864 --> 00:07:22,320
Nigga, they hadn't even put that man in a car yet and he was already
winning something. Vesper announced the rules. The track had two
paths. Each driver controlled a gate on the other person's route. To
reach the finish first, a claimant could close their partner's passage
and take the central lane.

21
00:07:22,570 --> 00:07:42,666
If both kept the gates open, neither would reach the prize before the
countdown ended. "So the rules are be a shitty husband or lose?" I
asked. "The rules are as stated," Zero said. "Then you stated some
shitty rules." I got into the car. Shawna settled her shoulders,
smiling across at me.

22
00:07:42,916 --> 00:08:05,728
"You trust me?" "Nigga, you drove me off another nigga's hood this
morning. We established that." The lights changed. We moved. At first
the cars were slow enough to feel insulting. Then the track steepened
and the little engines found their courage. Mirrors above us swung,
making the route look like it kept splitting into ten impossible
directions.

23
00:08:05,978 --> 00:08:29,085
I couldn't see Shawna after the first turn. I could hear her. "Right
gate!" I kept it open. "Your turn!" "Left!" Her gate opened before I
reached it. The spectators shouted. Some wanted us to win. Some wanted
us to choose wrong. Nigga, rich people will watch a marriage like it's
a horse race if you give them chairs and something cold to drink.

24
00:08:29,335 --> 00:08:47,358
The countdown appeared above the track. Thirty seconds. Ahead of me,
the central prize platform held two silver keys. One for the estate.
One for the opera house. The track bent away from it. I could see the
trick now. The gates weren't the only choice.

25
00:08:47,608 --> 00:09:10,635
The cars had been placed close enough to the platform that a driver
with more ambition than caution could reach it. Zero had counted on us
wanting the steering wheel more than each other. "Baby," I called. "I
see it." "You know which side?" "The pretty side." "Nigga, that's both
of mine." She laughed. We came out of opposite turns together. Twenty
seconds.

26
00:09:10,885 --> 00:09:33,380
I saw her face, the red dress tucked around her knees, the confidence
in her hands. I stood in the moving car. The crowd screamed. Zero
leaned forward. I jumped toward Shawna's car as she drew alongside. My
empty racer shot through the center lane and struck the low prize
platform. Silver keys flew up. I caught one.

27
00:09:33,630 --> 00:09:52,267
Shawna caught the other against her chest with one hand while keeping
the car straight with the other. Nigga, my wife caught an opera house
without letting go of the wheel. I landed half in her lap, half behind
the seat, all greatness and terrible posture. "Nigga, you heavy," she
said.

28
00:09:52,517 --> 00:10:14,542
"That's reputation." "Get your reputation out of my gearshift." "Baby,
your nigga trying to land with respect." "Land with your elbow on your
own side. I got a house to win." She drove us through the finish
together. The countdown stopped at eight. For a moment nobody knew
what to do with a rule that had been embarrassed in public.

29
00:10:14,792 --> 00:10:35,453
Then Lady Orsini stood up and clapped. "They both arrived!" Her
husband joined her. "And nobody divorced! Excellent round!" Somewhere
above us a man yelled, "That nigga caught the keys!" "That nigga's
wife caught hers too!" a woman shouted back. "He jumped out the car!"
"Nigga, she caught the husband.

30
00:10:35,703 --> 00:10:56,483
Keep up with the expensive part!" Shawna heard and lifted both keys,
then pointed at me. The woman clapped so hard her bracelets sounded
like a small crash of their own. The crowd erupted. I climbed out and
helped Shawna stand. Her hair had come loose. Her dress had a little
streak of grease near the hem.

31
00:10:56,733 --> 00:11:18,761
She held up the opera key like it had always been hers and the palace
had merely taken too long to find it. Zero descended the stairs. "You
abandoned your vehicle." "Nigga, I improved my company." "This was a
test of loyalty." "And that nigga in my seat was lonely. I brought him
back to his wife. You had mirrors everywhere.

32
00:11:19,011 --> 00:11:35,137
Don't tell me you missed the whole marriage." "The rules required—"
Vesper stepped between us. "A claimant and partner at the finish. They
are both here. The tokens were not surrendered. The gates remained
open." Zero looked at her.

33
00:11:35,387 --> 00:11:56,173
"You are becoming precise at unusual times." "You asked me to govern
the tournament." "I asked you to remember who governs you." The words
made the room colder. I moved beside her, not in front, because she
hadn't asked me to become a wall between her and her own decision.
"Nigga," I said, "she remembers plenty.

34
00:11:56,423 --> 00:12:22,900
That's your problem." He held my gaze, then smiled for the audience.
"The prizes are awarded." Applause. Relieved at first, then louder as
people decided which version of courage was safest to admit. Tank and
Rosa came out of their separate rooms a few minutes later carrying two
smaller prize boxes. "What happened?" I asked. Rosa opened hers. A
diamond bracelet. Tank opened his.

35
00:12:23,150 --> 00:12:45,941
A matching necklace. "They tried to make us argue," he said. "And?"
"Nigga, we already know how. We took the jewelry." Rosa tried the
bracelet on while Tank held the clasp. His fingers were too big for
the tiny catch. He frowned at it, tongue pressed against one corner of
his mouth, concentrating harder than I had seen him concentrate on men
with guns.

36
00:12:46,191 --> 00:13:08,240
Nigga, I said, you need backup? I'm fine. The jewelry putting up a
fight? Aiden. Rosa kept her arm still. Didn't laugh at him. Didn't
take it away and do it herself. She watched his face while the
strongest man in the room learned to make his hands small enough for
something she wanted to wear. Finally the clasp closed. Tank looked
up. There.

37
00:13:08,490 --> 00:13:25,741
Rosa turned her wrist. The diamonds caught the mirror light and threw
it back over both their faces. Beautiful, she said. He nodded at the
bracelet. Looks good on you. Nigga, I was talking to you. That
finished him. The man went quiet. Looked down.

38
00:13:25,991 --> 00:13:48,593
Looked up again like he wanted to make sure she'd said it in a room
with witnesses and wasn't going to take it back when he smiled too
much. Shawna squeezed my hand. Your brother. My nigga. He looks happy.
Nigga finally got somebody who can close an argument around his wrist.
Tank heard me and raised one finger without letting go of Rosa's hand.

39
00:13:48,843 --> 00:14:06,417
I respected the multitasking. Rosa kissed his knuckles, the ones I'd
seen break glass and men and expensive things bought by men who
thought they were safe behind them. Keep this pair, she told him. I
like what they do when you stop trying to scare everybody.

40
00:14:06,667 --> 00:14:30,908
He smiled at her so openly that one of the queens nearby put a hand
over her own husband's and held it there until he noticed. Nigga, we
were improving the whole fucking room. Mercedes and Porsche emerged
behind them with a furious prince between them. "What did y'all do?"
Shawna asked. "Made the nigga choose," Mercedes said. "Nigga chose
wrong," Porsche added.

41
00:14:31,158 --> 00:14:53,208
"I was presented with incomplete—" "Nigga, both women were standing in
front of you," Mercedes said. "How complete you need a bad decision?"
The prince opened his mouth. Both women looked at him. He closed it.
Outside, Vesper caught us at the bridge. For the first time since we'd
met her, she looked afraid without trying to turn it into elegance.

42
00:14:53,458 --> 00:15:14,479
"He knows something has changed." "A lot changed," I said. "I have
people in that palace. People he can hurt because I hesitate." "Then
we get your people out." "It is not that simple." "Nigga, I didn't ask
if simple had a room. I asked where your people sleeping tonight."
Vesper looked at me, then past me toward the palace.

43
00:15:14,729 --> 00:15:35,140
"He will count them." "Then let the nigga learn subtraction while we
find them beds." Shawna took the opera key out of my hand and put it
into Vesper's. "A whole building just became mine. Use the dressing
rooms. Use the stage. Use every stupid little balcony. Get them
there." Vesper stared at the key.

44
00:15:35,390 --> 00:15:53,959
"You have not even seen it." "Then make sure somebody waters the
flowers before I do." Nigga, my wife handed a queen a way out and
still made it sound like she was arranging opening night. Vesper
closed her fingers around the key. "Thank you." I looked back at the
shining palace.

45
00:15:54,209 --> 00:16:09,835
Zero stood in an upper window, a dark shape surrounded by reflections
of himself. I kissed Shawna on the bridge where he could see. Not for
him. Because the nigga had given me an excellent reason to remember
who kept winning.
